# Per-machine settings for airlock. Copy to deploy/airlock.env and edit.
#
#   cp deploy/airlock.env.example deploy/airlock.env
#
# deploy/airlock.env is NOT in git: it describes one machine. Everything here
# has a working default derived from the repository location, so an unedited
# file is a valid file — you only need to change what is actually different.

# ── Where the photo library lives ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# Every catalog: originals (in copy mode), derivatives, albums, deployments and
# received transfers. The directory that matters — back this one up.
# Default: <repo>/catalogs
#CATALOGS_HOST_DIR=/srv/airlock/catalogs

# The ingestion inbox, mounted read-write at /input.
# Default: <repo>/IN
#INPUT_HOST_DIR=/srv/airlock/IN

# The single root that storage routes are subpaths of, mounted READ-ONLY at
# /storage. A bind mount is fixed when the container starts, so a folder outside
# this root cannot be read whatever the UI says — make it wide enough to cover
# every library you will point a route at.
# Default: $HOME
#STORAGE_ROOT_HOST=/mnt/photos

# The application database (catalogs, users, storage routes). Small.
# Default: <repo>/systems/backend/database
#DATABASE_HOST_DIR=/srv/airlock/database

# ── Service addresses ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults route through the gateway by name. Change only if a service runs
# somewhere else.
#DEEPFACE_URL=http://deepface.airlock.lan
#ALBUMS_URL=http://albums.airlock.lan
#BACKEND_URL=http://backend.airlock.lan

# ── Browser origins ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The origins the backend accepts for credentialed requests and, more visibly,
# for the Socket.IO handshake. Derived automatically as airlock.lan + localhost
# + this machine's LAN address and short hostname, under http and https.
#
# Set this only when the UI is reached by an address none of those cover - a
# DNS name, a reverse proxy, a second interface. Getting it wrong is quiet: the
# UI loads and works, but never updates on its own.
#AIRLOCK_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://photos.example.com,http://photos.example.com

# ── Rootless podman ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Detected automatically: on rootless Linux this becomes
#   --userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000
# and on macOS it is empty. Set it here only to override that.
#
# Applies ONLY to the containers that run as uid 1000 (backend, deepface,
# vision, geoloc). The gateway, frontend and album-gallery run as root, where
# keep-id would remove the access they need.
#AIRLOCK_USERNS=

# ── Picture import ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# New storage routes get the streaming import (io_picture_import_v2_workflow.py).
# Uncomment to give them the previous, phased import instead.
#AIRLOCK_INGEST_SCRIPT=io_picture_import_workflow.py
#
# Optional tuning, passed to the backend only when set
# (documentation/features/ingestion-architecture.md §8):
#IMPORT_READERS=1              # fixed number of parallel reads; unset = adapt to the storage
#IMPORT_READ_CHUNK_MB=8
#IMPORT_META_CONCURRENCY=4
#IMPORT_RENDER_CONCURRENCY=3
#IMPORT_VIDEO_PRESET=veryfast   # x264 preset when the import makes previews itself
#IMPORT_VIDEO_NICE=10           # their niceness; 0 = none
#IMPORT_DEFER_VIDEO_RENDER=1    # video previews after every file is in
#IMPORT_RENDER_DURING_INGEST=0  # 1 = previews during ingest even on one spinning disk
#IMPORT_MOVE_RENAME=1           # move mode: rename into the catalog when the disk allows

# ── Accelerated services ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# documentation/specs/accelerated-services-spec.md. Where each GPU-capable
# service runs: auto | host | container | gpu | off.
#
#   auto, per platform and per service:
#                    DEEPFACE          TRANSCODE
#     macOS arm64    host (Metal)      host (VideoToolbox)
#     macOS x86_64   container *       host (VideoToolbox)
#     Linux x86_64   gpu or container  gpu or container
#     Linux arm64    container         container
#
#     * not a preference: TensorFlow publishes no macOS x86_64 wheel after 2.16
#       and this service needs >= 2.20, so natively it cannot be installed.
#
#   gpu needs an NVIDIA driver, a CDI spec and podman 4.1+; without them it
#   falls back to container and says so.
#
#   host needs things from THIS machine that a container image carries itself:
#   a Python >= 3.10 (3.12 is what the images use) and, for transcode, ffmpeg.
#   Without them, host also falls back to container with the reason - so a
#   missing host tool costs the accelerator, never the service. ./deploy/
#   deploy.sh reports both and builds the virtualenvs host mode needs.
#AIRLOCK_DEEPFACE_MODE=auto
#AIRLOCK_TRANSCODE_MODE=auto     # off = the import makes video previews itself
#
# The interpreter host mode builds its virtualenvs with. Unset = the newest
# python3.1x on PATH that is >= 3.10. NEVER bare `python3`: on macOS that is
# Apple's 3.9, which cannot install these requirements at all, and Homebrew
# does not create an unversioned python3 link.
#AIRLOCK_PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/bin/python3.12
#AIRLOCK_PYTHON_MIN=3.10
#
# backend-deepface memory. ON macOS CONTAINERS SHARE ONE VM, created with 2048 MB
# by default - not the Mac's memory. Each deepface worker holds its own copy of
# VGG-Face (~600 MB), so the worker count is sized from what a container can
# actually have, and below the floor the model warm-up is skipped so the service
# boots at all. More room for it:
#   podman machine stop && podman machine set --memory 6144 && podman machine start
#DEEPFACE_WORKERS=2              # unset = sized to the available memory
#DEEPFACE_WARMUP_EMBEDDER=1      # 0 = build VGG-Face on first use, not at boot
#AIRLOCK_DEEPFACE_MIN_MB=3072    # below this, the warm-up is skipped and said so
#YUNET_SCORE_THRESHOLD=0.9       # face detector cutoff; 0.85 finds ~39% more faces at
                                 # <1% false ones on `family` - see
                                 # documentation/features/FACE_DETECTION_THRESHOLD.md.
                                 # New scans only: scanned photos are not re-scanned.
#
# backend-transcode tuning:
#TRANSCODE_JOBS=2                # encodes at once
# auto = the best hardware encoder that actually works here, then software.
# Force one: libx264, h264_videotoolbox (macOS), h264_nvenc (NVIDIA closed
# driver), h264_qsv (Intel Quick Sync), h264_vaapi (Intel/AMD), h264_v4l2m2m
# (Raspberry Pi 4). Each is proved with a one-frame encode before use.
#TRANSCODE_ENCODER=auto
#TRANSCODE_VT_QUALITY=55         # VideoToolbox quality, 1-100 (spec section 9.1)
#TRANSCODE_VAAPI_DEVICE=/dev/dri/renderD128   # unset = probe every render node
#TRANSCODE_VAAPI_QP=23           # VA-API CQP quality; unset = follow the crf
#TRANSCODE_V4L2_BITRATE=2500k    # the Pi's encoder has no quality mode
#
# /dev/dri and /dev/video11 are passed into the container automatically when
# they exist. Rootless podman also needs the invoking user in the device's
# group, or every open inside the container is EACCES:
#   sudo usermod -aG render,video $USER      # then log out and back in
